DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261228
SUMMARY:▲ Long easy run 16 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic base…
DESCRIPTION:Long easy run 16 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic base is the lever
  - the fastest runners get there on Zone 1 volume. LONG RUN WITH A THRES
 HOLD FINISH: last 15 min at threshold EFFORT - HR 172-178\, which is 95-
 98% of your measured LTHR of 181. Provisional pace 5:35-5:50/km\; re-anc
 hor off the retest and do not chase a number that predates it. This is o
 ne of the four primary ways to move a lactate threshold\, and it doubles
  as durability work - running at pace on pre-fatigued legs is the 70.3 r
 un leg.\n\nWeek 7 of 11 - Sharpen\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. T
 alk test.\nSHARPEN. VO2max enters now the race is close - 3-5 min effort
 s\, the range where you accumulate real time at maximal oxygen uptake. B
 iggest running week of the block.\n14 days to Egmond 10.5 km / Venice ba
 se.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
