DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270103
SUMMARY:Easy run 5-6 km\, HR under 155. Third run of the…
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 5-6 km\, HR under 155. Third run of the week - short
  and genuinely easy.\n\nWeek 7 of 11 - Sharpen\nKeep HR under 158. Walk 
 the climbs. Talk test.\nSHARPEN. VO2max enters now the race is close - 3
 -5 min efforts\, the range where you accumulate real time at maximal oxy
 gen uptake. Biggest running week of the block.\n8 days to Egmond 10.5 km
  / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w7-s10-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261229
SUMMARY:Strength UPPER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength UPPER - push and pull as one session\, 45 min. Rows\
 , pull-ups\, overhead press\, rear delts. Heavy\, 4-6 reps\, not hypertr
 ophy ranges. Free against the running and cycling load. Dead hangs 3 x m
 ax at the end - grip is a genuine weakness at 32-36 s.\n\nWeek 7 of 11 -
  Sharpen\nSHARPEN. VO2max enters now the race is close - 3-5 min efforts
 \, the range where you accumulate real time at maximal oxygen uptake. Bi
 ggest running week of the block.\n13 days to Egmond 10.5 km / Venice bas
 e.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s0-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
SUMMARY:▲ Long easy run 12 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic base…
DESCRIPTION:Long easy run 12 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic base is the lever
  - the fastest runners get there on Zone 1 volume. LONG RUN WITH A THRES
 HOLD FINISH: last 15 min at threshold EFFORT - HR 172-178\, which is 95-
 98% of your measured LTHR of 181. Provisional pace 5:35-5:50/km\; re-anc
 hor off the retest and do not chase a number that predates it. This is o
 ne of the four primary ways to move a lactate threshold\, and it doubles
  as durability work - running at pace on pre-fatigued legs is the 70.3 r
 un leg.\n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. T
 alk test.\nSHARPEN then taper. Volume down 15%\, intensity held. Egmond 
 is Sunday of next week.\n7 days to Egmond 10.5 km / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s1-swim@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
SUMMARY:≈ Swim 45 min
DESCRIPTION:Swim 45 min - 600 m continuous\n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nSHA
 RPEN then taper. Volume down 15%\, intensity held. Egmond is Sunday of n
 ext week.\n7 days to Egmond 10.5 km / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s2-strides@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270106
SUMMARY:VO2MAX 4 x 4 min at VO2max EFFORT (11 km)
DESCRIPTION:VO2MAX 4 x 4 min at VO2max EFFORT - provisional pace 5:05-5:2
 0/km\, HR at the END of each rep 186-193. HR lags 60-90 s so it cannot s
 teer a 3 min rep\; set it by pace\, confirm by the HR you finish on\, 3 
 min jog. Longer reps\, one fewer. Last hard session before Egmond. Warm 
 up 15 min\, cool down 10 min.\n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nSHARPEN then ta
 per. Volume down 15%\, intensity held. Egmond is Sunday of next week.\n5
  days to Egmond 10.5 km / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s3-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270107
SUMMARY:○ BIKE 40 min
DESCRIPTION:BIKE 40 min - sweet spot\, 3 x 10-12 min at 88-93% FTP (~132-
 140 W)\, 5 min easy between. The 90 km bike is over half a 70.3 by time.
 \n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nSHARPEN then taper. Volume down 15%\, intens
 ity held. Egmond is Sunday of next week.\n4 days to Egmond 10.5 km / Ven
 ice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s4-swim@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270107
SUMMARY:≈ SWIM LESSON (1-on-1\, 45 min). Book 6-10 of these
DESCRIPTION:SWIM LESSON (1-on-1\, 45 min). Book 6-10 of these - highest-R
 OI line item in the whole season. You cannot self-coach a catch you have
  never felt.\n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nSHARPEN then taper. Volume down 
 15%\, intensity held. Egmond is Sunday of next week.\n4 days to Egmond 1
 0.5 km / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:egmond105kmvenicebase-w8-s5-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T190549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270108
SUMMARY:◆ Strength LOWER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength LOWER - HEAVY\, 45 min. Trap-bar deadlift 4 x 3 at 8
 8-92% 1RM (from 85 x 5 at 2 RIR your 1RM is ~105 kg\, so work at 92-97 k
 g - autoregulate\, add 2.5 kg when the last triple moves well). Then Bul
 garian split squat 3 x 5/leg heavy\, and calf raises 3 x 8 loaded. COMPL
 EX PAIRING: after each heavy set\, 5 box jumps or 20 m of bounds within 
 2 min - heavy resistance plus plyo beats either alone for running econom
 y. Heavy loads at or above 90% 1RM give greater economy gains than light
 er ones\, and the effect needs 10-14 weeks\, which is exactly this block
 . LOWER-LEG AND FOOT\, 5 min: tibialis anterior raises 3 x 15-20\, heel 
 walks 2 x 20 m\, eccentric dorsiflexion 3 x 10\, short-foot holds 3 x 30
  s per side.\n\nWeek 8 of 11 - Sharpen\nSHARPEN then taper. Volume down 
 15%\, intensity held. Egmond is Sunday of next week.\n3 days to Egmond 1
 0.5 km / Venice base.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
